Description: Use the session management protocol without GDK_DEBUG=session-mgmt.
 GDK 4.22 binds xx_session_manager_v1 only when GDK_DEBUG contains session-mgmt, so an application which turns
 on state saving still does not name its windows to the compositor. Upstream dropped the debug flag on main, after
 GDK had moved to the final protocol, xdg_session_manager_v1. This is the same change for the draft protocol 4.22
 speaks, which mutter offers through patches/mutter/xx-session-management.patch. GDK only binds the protocol, and
 only an application with GtkApplication:support-save sends anything over it.
Author: Adrian Vovk <adrianvovk@gmail.com>
Origin: backport, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/commit/15da56ccc5cf225bed58885a5997c16f0af7b679
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-04
